# What NOT to upload when deploying tristatetags.com.
#
# Vercel uses this INSTEAD of .gitignore once it exists, so everything
# .gitignore covered has to be repeated here or it would start being uploaded.
#
# The build is `npm run build` -> dist/ and it only ever reads src/, public/,
# api/, index.html and the config files in this directory. Nothing excluded
# below is part of that.
#
# Every file pattern here is ROOT-ANCHORED with a leading slash, deliberately.
# A bare `*.jpg` also matches src/assets/hero-bg.jpg and public/reviews/*.jpg;
# a bare `*.mp3` matches src/assets/audio/tokyo-drift.mp3, which
# src/components/BackgroundMusic.tsx imports -- so the unanchored forms would
# have stripped the hero image, the review photos, and failed the build.

# --- everything .gitignore already covered ---
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*
.vscode/*
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
server/data
.vercel

# --- secrets. Never served, but they have no business in a build upload ---
.env
.env.*

# --- other projects that merely share this folder ---
# Separate deployments with their own pipelines. The tag site's build never
# reads a line of them, and together they are the bulk of the upload.
/system/
/v2/
/krabinsurancebot/
/supabase/
/driver-hiring-kit/
# NOT /admin/ -- package.json's `prebuild` runs scripts/sync-admin-to-backend.mjs,
# which copies admin/index.html and admin/app.js into public/backend/. Excluding
# it fails the build outright, which is exactly what it did the first time.

# --- loose files sitting in the repo root ---
# Real customers' documents among them; none of it is referenced by the build.
/*.pdf
/*.jpg
/*.mp3
/*.zip
/*.code-workspace
/debug.log
/.claude/
/.cursor/
